@startuml
title weefs — High-level Good Design (patterns introduced to fix the bad design)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

' =====================================================================
' UI layer — MVC restored, multi-session, interface-driven
' =====================================================================
package "UI (clean MVC, multi-session)" #E8F5E9 {

  class MainFrame <<GOOD: depends on interface>> {
    -controller : IArchiveController
    -model : ArchiveModel
  }
  note right of MainFrame
    View depends on IArchiveController,
    not the concrete controller class.
    Was: held concrete ArchiveController.
  end note

  class ArchiveModel <<GOOD: session registry>> <<Observable>> {
    -sessions : List<MountSession>
    -activeSession : MountSession
    -fileSystemFactory : FileSystemFactory
    -pcs : PropertyChangeSupport
    --
    +openArchive(Path, boolean) : void
    +openDirectory(Path, boolean) : void
    +openMountUri(URI, boolean) : void
    +setActiveSession(String) : void
    +closeSession(String) : void
    +setNfsConfig(NfsConnectionConfig) : void
  }
  note right of ArchiveModel
    No longer owns per-mount state.
    Holds a list of MountSession instances
    and delegates state to each.
    Was: single archive + NFS god object.
  end note

  class MountSession <<GOOD: Value Object>> <<Extract Class>> {
    -id : String
    -fileSystem : FileSystem
    -displayPath : Path
    -readOnly : boolean
    -remoteMounted : boolean
    -nfsConfig : NfsConnectionConfig
    +isSaveable() : boolean
    +close() : void
  }
  note bottom of MountSession
    All per-mount state (FS, path,
    read-only, remote flag, NFS config)
    now lives here.
    Enables multiple concurrent mounts.
  end note

  class RemoteMountManager <<GOOD: Extract Class>> {
    -nfsConfig : NfsConnectionConfig
    +setNfsConfig(NfsConnectionConfig) : void
    +isNfsMounted() : boolean
  }

  class ClipboardEntry <<GOOD: Value Object>> <<record>> {
    +node : FileNode
    +cut : boolean
    +sourceSessionId : String
  }
  note bottom of ClipboardEntry
    New abstraction enabling copy/cut/paste
    across sessions (sourceSessionId routes
    reads to the correct backend).
    Was: no clipboard at all.
  end note

  interface IArchiveController <<GOOD: ISP>>
  interface INfsController    <<GOOD: ISP>>
  class ArchiveController <<GOOD: single source of truth>> {
    -model : ArchiveModel
    -fileOps : IFileOperations
    -nfsFileOps : IFileOperations
    -clipboard : ClipboardEntry
    --
    +getFileOps() : IFileOperations
    +copySelected() : void
    +cutSelected() : void
    +pasteSelected() : void
    +saveSession(String) : void
    +closeSession(String) : void
  }
  IArchiveController <|.. ArchiveController
  INfsController    <|.. ArchiveController

  interface IFileOperations <<GOOD: DIP>> {
    +createDir(String) : void
    +delete(FileNode) : void
    +rename(FileNode, String) : void
    +extract(FileNode, Path) : void
  }
  class FileOperations
  class NfsFileOperations
  IFileOperations <|.. FileOperations
  IFileOperations <|.. NfsFileOperations
  note top of IFileOperations
    Seam introduced so the controller
    can be unit-tested and can swap
    between local and NFS backends.
    Was: concrete FileOperations /
    NfsFileOperations returned directly.
  end note

  ArchiveModel "1" o-- "*" MountSession
  ArchiveModel --> RemoteMountManager
  ArchiveController --> ArchiveModel
  ArchiveController --> IFileOperations
  ArchiveController --> ClipboardEntry
  MainFrame --> IArchiveController

  ' --- supporting base classes (unchanged across transition) ---
  class FileNode <<base: tree node>> {
    -name : String
    -path : Path
    -directory : boolean
    -children : List<FileNode>
  }
  class FileType <<base: enum>>
  class FileTypeDetector <<base: util>>
  class ArchiveTreePanel <<base: view>>
  class FileContentPanel <<base: view>>
  class StatusBarPanel <<base: view>>
  class MenuBarFactory <<base: view builder>>
  class ToolBarFactory <<base: view builder>>
  class IconFactory <<base: util>>
  class SwingUtils <<base: util>>
  class WeeFsApp <<base: entry>>
  class NfsConnectionConfig <<base: value object>>
  class NfsConnectionDialog <<base: view>>
  class PropertiesDialog <<base: view>>
  class AboutDialog <<base: view>>

  WeeFsApp --> ArchiveModel
  WeeFsApp --> ArchiveController
  WeeFsApp --> MainFrame
  WeeFsApp ..> SwingUtils
  MainFrame --> ArchiveTreePanel
  MainFrame --> FileContentPanel
  MainFrame --> StatusBarPanel
  MainFrame ..> MenuBarFactory
  MainFrame ..> ToolBarFactory
  MainFrame ..> AboutDialog
  MainFrame ..> PropertiesDialog
  MainFrame ..> NfsConnectionDialog
  ArchiveTreePanel --> IArchiveController
  ArchiveTreePanel ..> FileNode
  ArchiveTreePanel ..> MountSession
  ArchiveTreePanel ..> IconFactory
  FileContentPanel ..> FileNode
  FileContentPanel ..> FileTypeDetector
  StatusBarPanel --> ArchiveModel
  MenuBarFactory ..> IArchiveController
  MenuBarFactory ..> INfsController
  ToolBarFactory ..> IArchiveController
  ToolBarFactory ..> INfsController
  FileTypeDetector --> FileType
  ArchiveModel --> FileNode
  MountSession --> NfsConnectionConfig
  ClipboardEntry --> FileNode
  NfsConnectionDialog ..> NfsConnectionConfig
}
' =====================================================================
package "Filesystem SPI (OCP + DIP)" #E8F5E9 {

  interface FileSystemDriver <<GOOD: SPI>> {
    +scheme() : String
    +open(URI, Map) : FileSystem
  }
  class FileSystemFactory <<GOOD: Open Factory>> {
    -drivers : Map<String, FileSystemDriver>
    +register(FileSystemDriver) : void
    +open(URI, Map) : FileSystem
  }
  class LocalFileSystemDriver
  class ZipFileSystemDriver {
    -provider : ExtZipFsProvider
    +ZipFileSystemDriver(ExtZipFsProvider)
  }
  class NfsFileSystemDriver {
    -provider : NfsSftpFsProvider
    +NfsFileSystemDriver(NfsSftpFsProvider)
  }
  note top of FileSystemFactory
    register(driver) makes the factory
    Open/Closed — new schemes plug in
    without modifying the factory.
    Was: hard-coded registerDefaults().
  end note
  note bottom of NfsFileSystemDriver
    Provider is constructor-injected (DIP).
    Was: new'd internally.
  end note

  FileSystemDriver <|.. LocalFileSystemDriver
  FileSystemDriver <|.. ZipFileSystemDriver
  FileSystemDriver <|.. NfsFileSystemDriver
  FileSystemFactory o--> FileSystemDriver
  ArchiveModel --> FileSystemFactory

  ' --- supporting base classes ---
  class ExtZipFileSystem <<base: weefs FS>>
  class ExtZipFsProvider <<base: weefs FS>>
  ZipFileSystemDriver --> ExtZipFsProvider
  ExtZipFsProvider --> ExtZipFileSystem
}

' =====================================================================
' Archive format — Strategy + Registry
' =====================================================================
package "Archive format (Strategy + Registry)" #E8F5E9 {

  interface ArchiveFormat <<GOOD: Strategy>> {
    +supports(Path) : boolean
    +extract(Path, Path) : void
    +write(Path, Path) : void
  }
  class TarArchiveFormat
  class ZipArchiveFormat
  class ArchiveFormats <<GOOD: Registry>> {
    +{static} FORMATS : List<ArchiveFormat>
  }
  class ArchiveFormatDetector <<GOOD: SRP>>
  class ArchiveFormatInfo <<Value Object>>
  enum ArchiveContainerType

  ArchiveFormat <|.. TarArchiveFormat
  ArchiveFormat <|.. ZipArchiveFormat
  ArchiveFormats o--> ArchiveFormat
  ArchiveFormats ..> ArchiveFormatDetector
  ArchiveFormatDetector --> ArchiveFormatInfo
  ArchiveFormatDetector --> ArchiveContainerType

  note bottom of ArchiveFormats
    Replaces the monolithic Extractor.
    Each format is its own Strategy;
    ArchiveFormats is a Registry of them.
  end note
}

' =====================================================================
' Compression — Strategy + Factory
' =====================================================================
package "Compression (Strategy + Factory)" #E8F5E9 {

  interface ICompressionStrategy <<GOOD: Strategy>> {
    +wrapInput(InputStream) : InputStream
    +wrapOutput(OutputStream) : OutputStream
  }
  class CompressionStrategyFactory <<GOOD: Factory>>
  class NoCompressionStrategy
  class GzipCompressionStrategy
  class Bzip2CompressionStrategy
  class XzCompressionStrategy
  class LzmaCompressionStrategy

  ICompressionStrategy <|.. NoCompressionStrategy
  ICompressionStrategy <|.. GzipCompressionStrategy
  ICompressionStrategy <|.. Bzip2CompressionStrategy
  ICompressionStrategy <|.. XzCompressionStrategy
  ICompressionStrategy <|.. LzmaCompressionStrategy
  CompressionStrategyFactory --> ICompressionStrategy

  note bottom of CompressionStrategyFactory
    Replaces inline "if (isGzip) ..." code.
    Each codec is a separate Strategy;
    the Factory picks one by magic header.
  end note
}

' =====================================================================
' NFS — transport isolated behind interface
' =====================================================================
package "NFS (isolated transport)" #E8F5E9 {

  interface IRemoteFileSystem <<GOOD: DIP>>
  class NfsFileSystem
  class NfsSftpFsProvider
  class NfsSftpFsIO <<utility>>
  NfsFileSystem ..|> IRemoteFileSystem
  NfsFileSystemDriver --> NfsSftpFsProvider
  NfsSftpFsProvider --> NfsFileSystem
  NfsSftpFsProvider ..> NfsSftpFsIO

  note bottom of IRemoteFileSystem
    Remote FS now implements a
    capability interface; callers
    depend on the interface, not JSch.
  end note
}

' =====================================================================
' Cross-package wiring
' =====================================================================
FileOperations ..> ArchiveFormats : <<extract/write>>
ArchiveFormats ..> ICompressionStrategy : <<Tar wraps via>>
ExtZipFileSystem ..> ICompressionStrategy : <<Zip entry wraps via>>
ExtZipFileSystem ..> ArchiveFormats
NfsFileSystem --> NfsFileSystemDriver : <<produced by>>
ExtZipFsProvider --> ZipFileSystemDriver : <<produced by>>

' =====================================================================
' Transition summary
' =====================================================================
legend right
  == Bad design  →  Good design ==
  God ArchiveModel            → ArchiveModel + MountSession + RemoteMountManager
  Single archive              → sessions : List<MountSession>, activeSession
  Duplicate currentNfsConfig  → single source of truth in MountSession
  Fat ArchiveController       → ArchiveController impl IArchiveController + INfsController (ISP)
  Concrete NfsFileOperations  → IFileOperations seam (DIP)
  View → concrete controller  → MainFrame → IArchiveController
  No clipboard                → ClipboardEntry record (cross-session copy/cut/paste)
  Hardcoded FileSystemFactory → FileSystemFactory.register(driver) + FileSystemDriver SPI (OCP)
  new'd providers in drivers  → constructor-injected providers (DIP)
  Monolithic Extractor        → ArchiveFormat Strategy + ArchiveFormats Registry + ArchiveFormatDetector
  Inline gzip/xz wrapping     → ICompressionStrategy + CompressionStrategyFactory
  JSch leaked to callers      → IRemoteFileSystem interface, NfsSftpFsIO hidden as utility
  No theming / deprecated UI  → FlatLaf L&F + theme-aware renderers
endlegend
@enduml
